      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ponderay’s name comes from the French words ‘Pend d’Oreille’, echoing the local indigenous people.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponderay%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Lake Pend Oreille, on which Ponderay sits, is a corruption of the same Pend d’Orielles.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponderay%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ponderay proudly carries the motto ‘Little City with the Big Future’ for its growing community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponderay%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ponderay’s original plat was filed in Kootenai County on May 5, 1904.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ponderay%2C_Idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The village incorporated on May 27, 1947, and became a city on November 26, 1968.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
